condition_name: Acute Otitis Media
condition_slug: acute-otitis-media
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: Acute inflammation of the middle ear due to pyogenic organisms.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[7]: Earache,Fever,Deafness,Ear discharge,"Malaise (in babies, irritability)",Redness of the eardrum,"Later, perforation and pulsating mucopurulent discharge"
investigations[2]: Ear swab for MCS - swab taken properly without contamination,FBC and Differentials
treatment:
  goals[2]: Control infection,Restore normal hearing
  non_drug[2]: Ear toileting and antiseptic dressings,Myringotomy for persistent mucopurulent collection in middle ear with bulging eardrum
  drug[13]: Antibiotics,"Amoxicillin - Adult: 500 mg -1 g orally 8 hourly for 5 - 7 days","Amoxicillin - Child: 40 mg/kg orally 8 hourly",Analgesics,"Paracetamol - Adult: 500 mg - 1 g orally 4 - 6 hourly (maximum of 4 g/d) for 5 - 7 days","Paracetamol - Child over 50 kg: same as adult dosing","Paracetamol - 6 - 12 years: 250-500 mg 4-6 hourly","Paracetamol - 1 - 5 years: 125 - 250 mg","Paracetamol - 3 months - 1 year: 125 - 250 mg for 5 - 7 days",Systemic decongestant,"Psuedoephedrine - Adult: 60 mg orally 4 – 6 hourly, (maximum 4 times a day)","Psuedoephedrine - Child 6-12 years: 30 mg (5 mL of syrup) 8 hourly","Psuedoephedrine - Child 2-5 years:15 mg, (2.5 mL of syrup) 4-8 hourly"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[2]: Preparations of pseudoephedrine with antihistamines may cause drowsiness,Avoid ear drops
  supportive_measures[1]: Bed rest and adequate fluids
differential_diagnoses[3]: Acute otitis externa,Referred otalgia,Otitis media with Effusion
complications[4]: Acute mastoiditis,Facial nerve paralysis,Labyrinthitis,"Intracranial (meningitis, brain abscess, lateral sinus thrombosis)"
prevention[1]: General healthy and clean airy environment reduces incidence of upper respiratory infections (colds)
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null